%description:

RFC 826 -- a station that is not the target of a broadcast request answers nothing.

Checks RFC826-RECV-5 from doc/project/evidence/standard/rfc826/catalog.md, and covers
RFC826-RECV-1. The English procedure is in
doc/project/evidence/protocol/arp/checks/input-validation.md#a-request-for-a-third-station;
the program steps below map onto its expected observations. Mapping of the shared link
mockup: host A = hostA, host B = hostB, host C = hostC, switch S = switch.

Host A resolves the address of host C. The request is a broadcast, so host B receives it
too, and host B takes the negative branch of the target question: end of processing, and the
packet is discarded. Host B runs no program and sends nothing of its own, so any packet from
host B would be an answer to this request.

Deviation: expected observation 2, that host C answers the request, is not a program step.
The absence watch of expected observation 3 has to cover the moment right after host B
receives the request, which is also the moment host C answers, and a greedy step consumes
its whole window. The answer of host C is asserted instead on the line that its program
prints at the end of the run: a datagram that arrived proves that the resolution completed,
and only a reply from host C could have completed it.

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "ArpMutations.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("rfc826_third_station_request")
        // Expected observation 1: the request reaches host B, and its target protocol
        // address is the address of host C and not of host B.
        .once(on("hostB.eth[0].mac").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
                  .packet("arp.opcode == 1")
                  .match([](const MatchContext& c) {
                      auto packet = c.event.packet;
                      return ipv4AddressField(packet, "arp.destIpAddress") == interfaceIpv4Address("hostC.eth[0]").str()
                             && ipv4AddressField(packet, "arp.destIpAddress") != interfaceIpv4Address("hostB.eth[0]").str();
                  })
                  .describe("the request for the address of host C, at host B's interface")
                  .within(0.5))
        // Expected observation 3: host B puts no ARP packet on the link (RFC826-RECV-5,
        // RECV-1).
        .never(on("hostB")
                  .match([](const MatchContext& c) { return arpPacketLeaves(c.event, "hostB"); })
                  .describe("any ARP packet from host B")
                  .within(0.85));
}

%activity:
// present only so opp_test compiles the %global above; this module is not in the network.
EV << "rfc826_third_station_request compiled\n";

%file: test.ned

import inet.node.ethernet.Eth100M;
import inet.node.ethernet.EthernetSwitch;
import inet.node.inet.StandardHost;
import inet.networklayer.configurator.ipv4.Ipv4NetworkConfigurator;

// The shared link mockup: three hosts on one Ethernet segment, joined by a switch.
network ArpSharedNet
{
    submodules:
        configurator: Ipv4NetworkConfigurator { @display("p=100,50"); }
        switch: EthernetSwitch { @display("p=400,150"); }
        hostA: StandardHost { @display("p=250,100"); }
        hostB: StandardHost { @display("p=250,250"); }
        hostC: StandardHost { @display("p=550,150"); }
    connections:
        hostA.ethg++ <--> Eth100M <--> switch.ethg++;
        hostB.ethg++ <--> Eth100M <--> switch.ethg++;
        hostC.ethg++ <--> Eth100M <--> switch.ethg++;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
network = ArpSharedNet
sim-time-limit = 1s
seed-set = 0

# One datagram of 100 octets from host A to host C. Host B runs no program.
*.hostA.numApps = 1
*.hostA.app[0].typename = "UdpBasicApp"
*.hostA.app[0].destAddresses = "hostC"
*.hostA.app[0].destPort = 5000
*.hostA.app[0].localPort = 4000
*.hostA.app[0].messageLength = 100B
*.hostA.app[0].startTime = 0.1s
*.hostA.app[0].sendInterval = 1s
*.hostC.numApps = 1
*.hostC.app[0].typename = "UdpSink"
*.hostC.app[0].localPort = 5000

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST rfc826_third_station_request: PASS

%contains: stdout
hostC.app[0]: received 1 packets
